# Accepted, time-boxed exception for the Trivy filesystem scan.
#
# CVE-2026-81726 / GHSA-8mgp-746c-j5xp: nltk "model-artifact APIs bypass pathsec".
# Every released nltk version (<= 3.10.3) is affected and no patched release exists
# yet, so there is nothing to upgrade to. The advisory covers
# TransitionParser.train/parse, AveragedPerceptron.save/load,
# PerceptronTagger.save_to_json and save_maxent_params. Nothing in the Inspect image
# calls them: inspect-evals uses nltk only for tokenizers, data lookup and BLEU.
# See adapters/inspect/requirements.txt and README.md ("Updating dependencies").
#
# The exception expires on the date below so it is re-evaluated; remove it as soon
# as a fixed nltk is released and requirements.txt is bumped.
CVE-2026-81726 exp:2026-12-31

# CVE-2026-104851: fsspec < 2026.6.0, ReferenceFileSystem template rendering (HIGH).
# The lm-eval adapter pins fsspec 2025.3.0 because datasets==3.6.0 caps it at
# <=2025.3.0, and datasets>=4 cannot load the dataset-loading scripts that 13 of its
# 214 benchmarks need (cmmlu_*, aclue_*, pile_*, ethics_cm, qasper_freeform). Nothing
# in the adapter, datasets, lm_eval or s3fs uses ReferenceFileSystem (grepped
# 2026-11-11), so the vulnerable code path is not reachable. See
# adapters/lm-eval/requirements.txt.
#
# The exception expires so it is re-evaluated. Remove it when lm-eval or the dataset
# owners make those tasks load without scripts and the adapter moves to datasets>=4.8.5
# (fsspec >= 2026.6.0). If that has not happened by the expiry date, drop the 13
# benchmarks and move to datasets>=4 instead of extending the exception.
CVE-2026-104851 exp:2027-01-31
